<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-7818] Incorrect assertion in PDS page eviction method</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-7818</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;There is an assertion in the method org.apache.ignite.internal.processors.cache.persistence.pagemem.PageMemoryImpl.Segment#removePageForReplacement:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;
&lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;assert&lt;/span&gt; relRmvAddr != INVALID_REL_PTR;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Which seems&#160;potentially dangerous. In some rare cases, when count of interations more then 40% of allocated pages and all processed pages are aquired, the&#160;&lt;tt&gt;relRmvAddr&lt;/tt&gt;&#160;variable will be uninitialized and &lt;tt&gt;AssertionException&lt;/tt&gt;&#160;will be thrown. But it&apos;s a correct case and page to evict can be found later in the method &lt;tt&gt;tryToFindSequentially.&lt;/tt&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
