                            <comment id="16484080" author="dpavlov" created="Tue, 22 May 2018 14:47:44 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;I&apos;m not sure I agree with fix, we still can&apos;t operate if we got invalid PTR after while execution.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16487080" author="dpavlov" created="Wed, 23 May 2018 11:05:22 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;I guess we need to bypass a litte bit more code in case of invalid ptr is placed in the variable, we need to fallback to full scan, but do not crash.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It is also desirable to reprocude this situation in some kind of PageMemoryUnit test with mocked other modules, so we could be sure this will never happen. But test is not simple, so it is up to you to write the test or do accurate code analysis.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For now, I cancel the patch.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16492840" author="alex_pl" created="Mon, 28 May 2018 17:21:11 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;I write a reproducer for this bug ( &lt;span class=&quot;nobr&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/attachment/12925446/12925446_PageMemoryPdsAssertTest.java&quot; title=&quot;PageMemoryPdsAssertTest.java attached to IGNITE-7818&quot;&gt;PageMemoryPdsAssertTest.java&lt;sup&gt;&lt;img class=&quot;rendericon&quot; src=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/images/icons/link_attachment_7.gif&quot; height=&quot;7&quot; width=&quot;7&quot; align=&quot;absmiddle&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; border=&quot;0&quot;/&gt;&lt;/sup&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;). It&apos;s realy not enough to just remove assertion. Instead, I think, we can  return &lt;tt&gt;tryToFindSequentially&lt;/tt&gt; if address is invalid.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
